WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Let's take a look inside Ellery. Here's the opportunity pipeline, with each pursuit organized by stage. This walkthrough uses sample records.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Open an opportunity to see the fit score and the reasoning behind it. Here, we can review the scope, deadlines, strengths, and action items before deciding whether to pursue.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Next, open Selection. Ellery starts with relevant projects from your firm's records. You can review the recommended examples and choose the work that best supports your case.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Scroll down to the proposed team. Each role connects to a person's experience on the selected projects, with alternatives available for review.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The experience matrix forms from those choices. Your team reviews the selections before approving the workflow.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:57.000
In Documents, the solicitation and amendments sit alongside the prepared sections. Resumes, the team chart, the experience matrix, and narratives are available in one place.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The Proposal tab shows which sections are ready and brings the package together. These are sample outputs. Your team checks the content and handles the final submission.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Behind every pursuit is your firm's project library. Search past work by name, location, or type to find the experience you need.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Personnel records bring qualifications and experience together too. Your people, your projects, and your next opportunity, connected in one workspace. That's Ellery.
